,"Blanketed by the main.":"ed2c2d9e8893.mp3","Boom on the centreline and the upper leech slightly open: the flow stays attached.":"ca831a605111.mp3","Boom on the centreline.":"afa5d39b72f4.mp3","Broad reach.":"b16b633d0d47.mp3","Check the sheet.":"7cccd131f575.mp3","Close reach.":"bc34a5989a55.mp3","Close-hauled, the windward one can lift now and then.":"81dd4138cbb5.mp3","Close-hauled.":"60a8cc0b17d5.mp3","Correct early and small and let the stern follow the wave.":"669e94bdd097.mp3","Crew to leeward: with a little heel the boat picks up some helm and gives better feel.":"6fd39e956884.mp3","Cunningham.":"ca5990b73766.mp3","Dead run.":"d2597f9ee178.mp3","Depth in the lower part = power.":"ccdfe3a553f0.mp3","Do not let the main out against the shrouds.":"806c8d8470fa.mp3","Do not point so high: speed first, then height.":"c2f0d311e262.mp3","Downwind a blanketed genoa adds nothing and snaps.":"1eeffe613e31.mp3","Downwind, reef before you bear away: you have to head up to reef.":"266de4fbee7b.mp3","Drop the traveller to leeward.":"cd904e51d51c.mp3","Ease the backstay adjuster.":"efb18afe0efe.mp3","Ease the cunningham.":"d251e810aa0f.mp3","Ease the halyard a little.":"813f8530bc9a.mp3","Ease the mainsheet in the gust.":"c5e49422aa4b.mp3","Ease the outhaul a little.":"f9c937f82904.mp3","Ease the sheet in gusts with the vang on.":"324783c52182.mp3","Ease the vang in the gusts.":"db18780d57d1.mp3","Ease until it flutters, then trim in a touch.":"7af3e5bb0c07.mp3","Ease until the windward telltale lifts, then trim in a touch.":"3fd45c57a1e0.mp3","Eased a little compared with close-hauled.":"a186db8396b5.mp3","Eased almost to the shrouds, without the sail resting on them.":"2551b4b795b0.mp3","Eased: a few light wrinkles in the luff do not matter.":"9455766136b3.mp3","Eased: more depth, more power.":"4724b9dab5bf.mp3","Even if it flutters.":"835656170c6a.mp3","Feather up in the gusts.":"628446203069.mp3","Fixed: if the top breaks before the bottom you cannot correct it; compensate with the sheet.":"94ec92c11003.mp3","Flatten the main.":"0479fa2c22e4.mp3","Flattens the lower third of the main.":"1e8378df9948.mp3","Forward and, if you have a barber hauler or outboard track, outboard.":"9caea4dc0059.mp3","Forward: more depth down low.":"7938cc20e1ae.mp3","Full sail.":"0f1a96cdc641.mp3","Furl more genoa.":"609783df0d5a.mp3","Furl some of the genoa.":"24b7c06104e4.mp3","Furl the genoa.":"c77fe880dfb4.mp3","Furler.":"45ca38565779.mp3","Genoa":"61f3a9352c09.mp3","Genoa car slightly aft.":"c68b65d523ad.mp3","Genoa car.":"b07ac00580bb.mp3","Genoa with more depth low down.":"b4b053a808f1.mp3","Goal: both horizontal.":"1acfaa64e09a.mp3","Goose-wing it on the pole: to windward, opposite the main.":"56e55839b6ea.mp3","Goose-wing the genoa on the pole.":"525db59976b7.mp3","Half eased: ease until the luff starts to flutter, then trim in a touch.":"c67a27776aad.mp3","Halyard.":"4d25c1a689f2.mp3","Hard on: flattens the lower third.":"59f35ee37f35.mp3","Head to wind.":"425a68990943.mp3","Head up a little as you meet the wave and bear away to pick up speed going down it.":"669d08e4ece2.mp3","Head up a little or ease the sheet.":"d3ba1b9892e6.mp3","Head up a touch as the gust hits, until the genoa luff starts to flutter, and bear away again once it passes.":"ca317947a3f9.mp3","Head up on the way up, bear away on the way down.":"9334bd29ce3e.mp3","Heeling too much / struggling.":"4f4674961d26.mp3","If it does not stop.":"1169078400a9.mp3","If the bottom one breaks before the top: car aft.":"6ce47e04f1ce.mp3","If the top one breaks before the bottom: car forward.":"bf7243498204.mp3","If with the first one you are still over-heeling or carrying a lot of helm.":"f9d06cd0a690.mp3","If you are carrying lots of helm all the time, the boat is asking you to reduce sail.":"48243fd832f9.mp3","If you are still reefed from earlier, you no longer need to be.":"8a4d6f7c426a.mp3","In every gust, before touching the sheet: the boom moves out without the leech opening.":"48540c15447c.mp3","In gusts, drop the traveller or ease a hand-width so you do not over-heel.":"5e04a330a380.mp3","In strong gusts, ease it to spill pressure.":"0635a4ad9e46.mp3","In strong wind downwind it comes first.":"ed0cc023e4d0.mp3","In waves you cannot point as high: look for speed.":"8c8b2f707af1.mp3","It is fine for the front of the main to be backwinded by the genoa: you shed power without losing your course.":"1c40f6c73470.mp3","It is the fastest way to avoid a round-up off the wind.":"629bfad3c69d.mp3","It opens the upper leech and releases the pressure that lays the boat over.":"5a3474afb780.mp3","It prevents an accidental gybe.":"55bf0f382ba7.mp3","It rounds up because the main pushes the stern to leeward.":"f7baa944864f.mp3","Just enough to stop it vibrating.":"a0b2c41c6254.mp3","Keep the boom from lifting: if the top opens up, the boat rolls.":"d2286176f24e.mp3","Keeps rounding up.":"06ad98110d14.mp3","Last step for the main.":"dfdbab3cabfb.mp3","Leech flutters or vibrates.":"6f70c272bffc.mp3","Leeward telltale flutters.":"b16b4cabbafe.mp3","Less genoa if it is full and the main is reefed.":"1988a27893e5.mp3","Let the main luff flutter in gusts.":"d1917c09cb5b.mp3","Lets the boom out as far as possible.":"6ab2e9250dae.mp3","Lifejackets on and jacklines rigged.":"bfd460812115.mp3","Light wrinkles in the luff are fine in light air.":"58da695983fa.mp3","Luff and outhaul tight, and backstay adjuster on.":"03eb3cf08b79.mp3","Luff and outhaul tight.":"221208ee808e.mp3","Main":"008409d10176.mp3","Mainsheet slightly eased: copes better with changes in speed.":"fbaf08296c03.mp3","Medium: no wrinkles along the foot.":"4e20c8e0991e.mp3","Moderately on: stops the boom lifting and the boat rolling.":"2c1fa944d614.mp3","More depth in the sails.":"3853534ebfb3.mp3","More depth low down in the genoa.":"b89f43389964.mp3","More depth.":"7ea43baa02af.mp3","More main.":"9db9fe53a0b4.mp3","Move the car forward as you furl.":"fd2dea502788.mp3","Move the car forward.":"ea3858e81fa8.mp3","Move the genoa car aft.":"bbd8a879c078.mp3","Move the genoa car forward.":"486582a66606.mp3","Neutral: when you head up, the top and bottom telltales break together.":"6c00dd82bae3.mp3","No need to reduce sail for now.":"2202798d9c07.mp3","No reefs left: furl the genoa.":"43c802bd67da.mp3","No reefs.":"285684d9c231.mp3","No traveller: to depower, ease the sheet and control the leech with the vang.":"5c2f0300a0f6.mp3","Off the wind people tend to over-trim.":"43e8e1c91752.mp3","Off the wind you will get more heel and rolling.":"44559e5158b1.mp3","Off the wind, turn the bow away from the wind as the gust arrives and come back to course once it passes.":"16364be6d698.mp3","Off.":"340a8bb8e037.mp3","Old or stretched sail: it is wear, not trim.":"05ef65ddea4b.mp3","On a masthead rig it barely affects the main: it stops the forestay sagging so the genoa sets flatter.":"57365489ce07.mp3","On a masthead rig the genoa is the main engine: reducing it first cuts heel without leaving the boat with weather helm.":"f94cf2d7e120.mp3","On.":"13840dd1b22a.mp3","On: moves the depth forward and opens the upper leech.":"cfb8e6758599.mp3","On: no wrinkles, depth forward.":"2563ff13dcab.mp3","On: without a traveller, it is what holds the leech when you ease the sheet.":"c788ca78f3bf.mp3","Open the leech (twist).":"8d45d2305350.mp3","Opens the top of the genoa.":"effd9620f7f2.mp3","Opens the upper leech of the genoa and spills pressure up high.":"f4e15246034b.mp3","Outhaul hard on.":"7ee4d2eef90c.mp3","Outhaul slightly eased and backstay adjuster off: the sail drives harder through the waves.":"7598593d659b.mp3","Outhaul slightly eased: the sail drives harder through the waves.":"0d4cf3acbcd9.mp3","Outhaul.":"01893e2b7fcf.mp3","Overdo it and the leech hooks to windward and slows you down.":"dbb0c9ef1c5f.mp3","Point of sail.":"1e2ee8068578.mp3","Reduce in stages.":"dcb181c0cbb1.mp3","Reduce the main to cut heel and helm load.":"c8a46dcc6cff.mp3","Reducing it first restores balance to the helm.":"d071d6131c2d.mp3","Rig a boom preventer.":"91a8e647d57d.mp3","Roughly a third (approx.).":"821aed989bc4.mp3","Set so the top does not twist open too much.":"9a1cd3e7aef0.mp3","Shake out reefs and unfurl.":"4d5ed9defa7e.mp3","Sheet.":"587301d53269.mp3","Slack taken up, not pulling.":"e5f48b4f5014.mp3","Slams into waves and stops.":"a57d3ecf90c0.mp3","Slight heel in light air.":"4d3a44c27f3f.mp3","Slightly eased: depth low down.":"c0c9a2339cbc.mp3","Slightly eased: light wrinkles in the luff.":"2578da9b4460.mp3","Slow, lacks power.":"82a591ec7cbc.mp3","Steer with the waves.":"c98dc23997f2.mp3","Step 1.":"4beb6baee0bb.mp3","Step 10.":"b8bc8ee96908.mp3","Step 11.":"4e1d6a2a9dc7.mp3","Step 12.":"73976a395da7.mp3","Step 13.":"df1099546f8c.mp3","Step 2.":"3b53b5d8605c.mp3","Step 3.":"c5653dbfb3c9.mp3","Step 4.":"87d047eb6ed2.mp3","Step 5.":"4e2dd59ac645.mp3","Step 6.":"6308462fd0e5.mp3","Step 7.":"b76ee0a02447.mp3","Step 8.":"0bee0175ed1d.mp3","Step 9.":"a03a3d9165db.mp3","Still struggling: change the plan.":"482847c4b2c1.mp3","Stop a little short; resting on them it chafes and pushes the boat towards a round-up.":"9f4c68150a01.mp3","Take the 1st reef in the main.":"60caeedfae94.mp3","Take the 2nd reef.":"8d0f9f3a115c.mp3","Take the 3rd reef.":"1fcb5181af5b.mp3","Tension the backstay adjuster.":"c1f45a7b17c5.mp3","Tension the cunningham.":"d2f02c1cb212.mp3","Tension the main halyard.":"afe3a28239e4.mp3","That is good trim.":"416ec50d1252.mp3","The leeward one flutters: you are sailing too low or the sail is over-trimmed and the flow is stalling.":"79d2bcfccd75.mp3","The sheet lead is too far aft and the top twists open too much.":"fb2761cf5e25.mp3","The sheet lead is too far forward.":"b3ac152fff14.mp3","The vang stops the boom lifting and the sail bagging out.":"353df7c12dd8.mp3","The windward one flutters: you are pointing too high or the sail is eased too far.":"c8ea29f3e45d.mp3","Tight luff: the depth moves forward and the upper leech opens and spills pressure.":"43bedb7047ce.mp3","Tighten the leech line.":"f36834337dec.mp3","To half or less (approx.); a heavily furled genoa loses shape, which is why it comes last.":"6a1e403230f0.mp3","To leeward: drop it in each gust before touching the sheet.":"b956533b1759.mp3","To reef you have to head up almost to close-hauled and the apparent wind jumps: do it before it builds further.":"dfc495dd96f0.mp3","To windward: centre the boom with the sheet slightly eased.":"1ecab2057492.mp3","Traveller all the way to leeward.":"3d985b86abb4.mp3","Traveller to windward, sheet slightly eased.":"ef440dfed507.mp3","Traveller.":"af410122b3af.mp3","Trim back in once it passes.":"d891697cd799.mp3","Trim the sheet and bring the traveller to windward: the main pushes the bow into the wind.":"c5af9b66b69e.mp3","Trim the sheet: the main pushes the bow into the wind.":"80dad1a75e88.mp3","Trimmed in, but not too hard: let the top twist open a little.":"fe38cce80a2b.mp3","Trimmed in.":"8ad317fae4a3.mp3","Trimmed in: boom near the centreline and the top leech telltale streaming most of the time.":"ebf215a0331c.mp3","Trimmed until the leech is a few centimetres off the spreader and the telltales stream horizontally.":"5594710ecd52.mp3","Vang on (moderately).":"3588006ebee3.mp3","Vang.":"1b6a140dc14c.mp3","Well eased: ease until the luff starts to flutter, then trim in a touch.":"0fafe2acba86.mp3","When you furl, move the car forward because the clew rises and moves forward.":"6fe63f5d9a7a.mp3","Windward telltale flutters.":"30b8156dd2a8.mp3","With the wind on the quarter, do not go dead downwind: risk of gybing.":"09abd46342fd.mp3","Without a pole, goose-winging is unstable: furl it or come up to a broad reach.":"fb4ae29e0335.mp3","Without a traveller, the sheet is your release valve.":"287b56641de5.mp3","Without a vang, the boom lifts when you ease the sheet and the top of the sail opens.":"45ff9ffb1fa3.mp3","You are in the no-go zone.":"b5cae4d17527.mp3","Your boat has no reefs: furl genoa